(BAS-24 - undocumented precision on BAS-16/BAS-19: the manual says "blank
 line", and a line of nothing but SPACES counts as one - it closes the
 definition of `greet`, so the call and the statement after it are
 top-level. A COMMENT-only line does not: `chatter` is never closed, so
 `chatter.` and `Print "unreachable"` are absorbed into its own body and
 nothing after the signature ever runs. Only the first half produces
 output.
 The compiler warns about the second half at compile time - the same
 still-open-at-end-of-file warning as BAS-21 - so the difference between
 the two halves is diagnosed, just not at runtime.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-24.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   hi
   after the spaces-only line
)
To greet.
    Print "hi".
   
greet.
Print "after the spaces-only line".

To chatter.
    Print "chat".
(a comment where the paragraph break would go)
chatter.
Print "unreachable".
